{"type":"new","contents":"import Mathlib.NumberTheory.EulerProduct.DirichletLSeries\nimport InfoGeometry.Experimental.WeylDenominator\n\nopen scoped BigOperators\nopen Complex\n\nnamespace InfoGeometry.Canonical\n\n/-- The exact prime gas partition structure matching the physics readout. -/\nstructure PrimeGasPartition where\n  convergenceDomain : ℂ → Prop\n  partitionFunction : ℂ → ℂ\n  eulerProduct      : ℂ → ℂ\n\n/-- \n  The specialization gate. Notice we use the exact `↑↑p` double coercion:\n  Nat.Primes → ℕ → ℂ, which prevents subtype elaboration failures.\n-/\nstructure PrimeWeightSpecialization (P : PrimeGasPartition) where\n  partition_eq_eulerProduct :\n    ∀ s, P.partitionFunction s = P.eulerProduct s\n  eulerProduct_eq_prime_tprod :\n    ∀ s, P.eulerProduct s = ∏' (p : Nat.Primes), (1 - ↑↑p ^ (-s))⁻¹\n\n/-- The exact arithmetic bridge wrapping Mathlib's Dirichlet owner theorem. -/\ntheorem zeta_trace_bridge {s : ℂ} (hs : 1 < s.re) :\n    (∏' (p : Nat.Primes), (1 - ↑↑p ^ (-s))⁻¹) = riemannZeta s := by\n  simpa using riemannZeta_eulerProduct_tprod hs\n\n/-- Compatibility alias for the Weyl denominator bridge. -/\ntheorem weyl_denominator_limit_eq_zeta {s : ℂ} (hs : 1 < s.re) :\n    ∏' (p : Nat.Primes), (1 - ↑↑p ^ (-s))⁻¹ = riemannZeta s :=\n  zeta_trace_bridge hs\n\n/-- The final Klein-Hestenes invariant readout. -/\ntheorem PrimeWeightSpecialization.partitionFunction_eq_riemannZeta\n    {P : PrimeGasPartition}\n    (W : PrimeWeightSpecialization P)\n    {s : ℂ}\n    (hs : 1 < s.re) :\n    P.partitionFunction s = riemannZeta s := by\n  rw [W.partition_eq_eulerProduct s, W.eulerProduct_eq_prime_tprod s, zeta_trace_bridge hs]\n\n/-! ### Certified canonical constructor -/\n\n/--\nThe canonical `PrimeGasPartition` instance:\n- `convergenceDomain s := 1 < s.re`\n- `partitionFunction s := ∏' p : Nat.Primes, (1 - ↑↑p ^ (-s))⁻¹`\n- `eulerProduct s      := ∏' p : Nat.Primes, (1 - ↑↑p ^ (-s))⁻¹`\n\nBoth compute fields are definitionally the same tprod so that the\n`PrimeWeightSpecialization` below is constructed by `rfl`.\n-/\nnoncomputable def canonicalPrimeGasPartition : PrimeGasPartition where\n  convergenceDomain s := 1 < s.re\n  partitionFunction s := ∏' (p : Nat.Primes), (1 - ↑↑p ^ (-s))⁻¹\n  eulerProduct s      := ∏' (p : Nat.Primes), (1 - ↑↑p ^ (-s))⁻¹\n\n/--\nCertified `PrimeWeightSpecialization` for `canonicalPrimeGasPartition`.\nBoth fields are `rfl`; the analytic readback lives in\n`canonicalPartition_eq_riemannZeta`.\n-/\ndef canonicalPrimeWeightSpecialization :\n    PrimeWeightSpecialization canonicalPrimeGasPartition where\n  partition_eq_eulerProduct _s := rfl\n  eulerProduct_eq_prime_tprod _s := rfl\n\n/--\nCertified readback: `canonicalPrimeGasPartition.partitionFunction s = riemannZeta s`\nfor `1 < s.re`.  Proved via the specialization chain, using `riemannZeta_eulerProduct_tprod`\nonly at the final step.\n-/\ntheorem canonicalPartition_eq_riemannZeta {s : ℂ} (hs : 1 < s.re) :\n    canonicalPrimeGasPartition.partitionFunction s = riemannZeta s :=\n  canonicalPrimeWeightSpecialization.partitionFunction_eq_riemannZeta hs\n\nend InfoGeometry.Canonical\n","mtime":1778328887901}